    "title": "St. Pete sees recent spike in e-bike crashes - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kailey Tracy ,\n6 hours ago ST PETERSBURG, Fla. - Law enforcement says they’ve seen a spike in e-bike crashes across the area lately. Deputies in Pinellas County are investigating an e-bike crash that left a 67-year-old man with life-threatening injuries. Investigators say the man riding the e-bike didn’t stop at a stop sign and collided with a truck in Dunedin Tuesday. This crash unfortunately isn’t alone. Officials say the number of e-bike crashes continues to go up across the Bay Area. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
